WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.160
Here's a fact almost no parent hears

00:02.280 --> 00:03.120
until it's too late.

00:03.600 --> 00:05.440
If a 16 year old signs a professional

00:05.520 --> 00:07.840
contract with a club, he can never play

00:07.920 --> 00:09.200
college soccer again.

00:09.680 --> 00:10.800
Not a reduced scholarship.

00:11.120 --> 00:12.160
Not a smaller program.

00:12.720 --> 00:13.120
Never.

00:13.520 --> 00:15.840
That door closes permanently, the moment

00:15.880 --> 00:16.640
the ink dries.

00:17.160 --> 00:19.440
I'm Bert Mahecha, founder of MFH Global

00:19.520 --> 00:21.120
Football, and I've spent enough years

00:21.200 --> 00:23.520
around this sport, as a player, a coach,

00:23.680 --> 00:25.600
and a club owner, to know that this rule

00:25.680 --> 00:27.200
catches good families off guard

00:27.280 --> 00:27.920
constantly.

00:28.320 --> 00:29.120
I think that's wrong.

00:29.520 --> 00:30.720
You should know this before you're

00:30.800 --> 00:32.880
excited, not after you're red flagged.

00:33.280 --> 00:34.640
Let's be honest about the numbers.

00:34.960 --> 00:36.560
Going professional in the United States

00:36.640 --> 00:38.480
is roughly a one percent outcome.

00:38.880 --> 00:40.400
That's not pessimism, that's just

00:40.480 --> 00:42.640
reality, and it's exactly why college

00:42.720 --> 00:44.720
soccer matters so much for most American

00:44.960 --> 00:45.200
players.

00:45.560 --> 00:48.160
A scholarship, an education, four more

00:48.240 --> 00:49.760
years to develop physically and

00:49.840 --> 00:51.680
mentally, all while still playing the

00:51.760 --> 00:52.640
game at a high level.

00:53.120 --> 00:54.960
For most families, that path is the

00:55.040 --> 00:56.960
actual win, even if it doesn't feel as

00:57.040 --> 00:59.120
exciting as a pro contract at sixteen.

00:59.600 --> 01:01.440
So when an opportunity to go pro early

01:01.560 --> 01:03.440
comes along, the question isn't just

01:03.440 --> 01:06.240
"should my son take this." It's "does my

01:06.320 --> 01:08.400
son understand that this decision cannot

01:08.480 --> 01:10.720
be undone." A sixteen year old, no

01:10.840 --> 01:12.720
matter how mature, isn't always thinking

01:12.840 --> 01:14.320
about what happens if the pro career

01:14.440 --> 01:16.080
doesn't pan out the way everyone hoped.

01:16.480 --> 01:17.520
That's what parents are for.

01:18.000 --> 01:20.160
That's what an honest agent is for too.

01:20.210 --> 01:21.520
I'm not telling you to say no to

01:21.600 --> 01:22.800
professional opportunities.

01:23.240 --> 01:25.120
Some players are genuinely ready, and

01:25.200 --> 01:26.640
for them, that's the right path.

01:27.040 --> 01:28.960
What I'm telling you is to know exactly

01:29.040 --> 01:30.800
what you're trading before you trade it.

01:31.240 --> 01:32.880
Ask what happens if it doesn't work out.

01:33.320 --> 01:35.040
Ask what the realistic timeline looks

01:35.160 --> 01:35.280
like.

01:35.720 --> 01:37.840
Ask whether this club, this contract,

01:38.160 --> 01:40.320
this moment, is worth giving up the door

01:40.400 --> 01:41.520
that college represents.

01:42.000 --> 01:43.760
My job isn't to push you toward whatever

01:43.840 --> 01:44.560
pays me more.

01:44.920 --> 01:46.160
It's to make sure you're making this

01:46.240 --> 01:48.240
decision with your eyes open, not

01:48.400 --> 01:49.920
finding out about the rule after it's

01:50.000 --> 01:51.680
already too late to change your mind.

01:52.080 --> 01:53.760
If your family is facing a decision like

01:53.920 --> 01:55.440
this, or you just want to understand

01:55.520 --> 01:57.120
your options before one comes along,

01:57.520 --> 01:58.640
book a free consultation.

01:59.000 --> 02:00.720
We'll walk through it together, in plain

02:00.800 --> 02:02.720
language, before anything is signed.
